    {
        "content": "<p>The cache seems to work now. But the ona environments seem to be generally unstable: After some time (in hours), github authentication fails in weird ways and I cannot push to my repos anymore!</p>",
        "id": 545833717,
        "sender_full_name": "Yaël Dillies",
        "timestamp": 1760884423
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I tried opening a PR in Ona, and it told me \"your organization requires an active subscription to use this feature. Go to Settings &gt; Billing to subscribe\".</p>\n<p>Should we just remove the \"Build in Ona\" button?</p>",
        "id": 599822267,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1780497573
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>As a data point: I was a heavy user of gitpod, but have had no luck with Ona (and probably had my review capacity halved as a result...). I'd be in favor of dropping the button at least from the PR template.</p>",
        "id": 599825070,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1780498200
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"421885\">@Joscha Mennicken</span> also suggested removing the button in a DM. We also briefly discussed whether it might make sense to replace it with a button for GitHub's codespaces -- there are some difficulties there related to the fact that you can't include the PR number in the PR template, but if this is something that people would use I could look into it.</p>",
        "id": 599826380,
        "sender_full_name": "Bryan Gin-ge Chen",
        "timestamp": 1780498485
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm not sure if everyone who would use codespaces is aware that codespaces exists and is set up, so either a button or some other kind of hint might be useful?</p>",
        "id": 599827182,
        "sender_full_name": "Joscha Mennicken",
        "timestamp": 1780498652
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The codespace button is already prominent on the standard PR page, so I don't think we need it in the template:</p>\n<p><img alt=\"image.png\" class=\"inline-image\" data-original-content-type=\"image/png\" data-original-dimensions=\"2534x908\" data-original-src=\"/user_uploads/3121/lYfb_98IOeE1IWoQvXRmSPki/image.png\" src=\"/user_uploads/thumbnail/3121/lYfb_98IOeE1IWoQvXRmSPki/image.png/840x560.webp\"></p>",
        "id": 599830133,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1780499248
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>We could put it in the readme though</p>",
        "id": 599830422,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1780499312
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It is already in the readme: <br>\n<img alt=\"image.png\" class=\"inline-image\" data-original-content-type=\"image/png\" data-original-dimensions=\"838x239\" data-original-src=\"/user_uploads/3121/z1X-06TtyAPAk2_ifUIDaiqC/image.png\" src=\"/user_uploads/thumbnail/3121/z1X-06TtyAPAk2_ifUIDaiqC/image.png/840x560.webp\"></p>",
        "id": 599830906,
        "sender_full_name": "Joscha Mennicken",
        "timestamp": 1780499415
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Sidenote: If the ona button is removed from PRs, it should probably also be removed from the readme (and the wording in the previous paragraph adjusted).</p>",
        "id": 599831011,
        "sender_full_name": "Joscha Mennicken",
        "timestamp": 1780499439
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think we can leave it in the readme, perhaps just less prominently. I think we should only delete it if we also delete the config</p>",
        "id": 599832235,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1780499720
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Should the gitpod/ona config be deleted? It looks like it may no longer be working out-of-the-box.</p>",
        "id": 599837220,
        "sender_full_name": "Joscha Mennicken",
        "timestamp": 1780500803
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I guess at this point it serves only as an advertisement to pay money to Ona for an AI tool, which I guess does render it useless</p>",
        "id": 599839742,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1780501341
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(unless of course there are other tools that piggy-back on the gitpod config)</p>",
        "id": 599839789,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1780501353
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I suspect those tools will have migrated to the devcontainer spec by now, which is also what codespaces uses. Ona also seems to use devcontainers by now: <a href=\"https://ona.com/docs/ona/configuration/migrate-from-classic#migrate-from-gitpod-classic-to-ona\">https://ona.com/docs/ona/configuration/migrate-from-classic#migrate-from-gitpod-classic-to-ona</a></p>",
        "id": 599840373,
        "sender_full_name": "Joscha Mennicken",
        "timestamp": 1780501500
    }
]